      "description": "Lean build caches, one orphan branch per package and toolchain, restored so a build starts warm. Declared here, on the folio that builds the Lean packages, rather than as a row in folio-assistant's special-branches.json (owner, 2026-10-03). MIGRATED 2026-10-05 (owner: \"migratez qou\") from the legacy `lake-cache/<member>` names: scripts/lib/lake-cache-family.sh writes the declared name and reads it first, falling back to `lake-cache/<member>`, whose branches are kept and never deleted (AGENTS.md rule 9). `lake-cache/` is where a member is mounted; the restore scripts untar into `.lake/`, which the dot-prefix guard forbids declaring.",
